{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76","id":1533463,"title":"Childcare Subsystem \ud83d\udc76","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-01T16:56:55-07:00","id":1533463,"title":"Childcare Subsystem \ud83d\udc76","content":"So I spent the last few months creating <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WmUA-quns4q7H1wp-hHiU1D010y2oat4ErX6YEIhlXk/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">a system to represent caring for small children</a> within the CofD framework, and the result is either the best idea I've ever had, or the dumbest; I really don't know which, I only know that it's finally more-or-less done and ready to see the light of day. Let me know what you think of it. Would you ever consider using these rules in your own chronicle? Do any of the actual parents out there have suggestions for how to make it better/more accurate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":6327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","user":"Super_Dave","date":". 04-03-2024, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T20:23:04-07:00","id":1533465,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't use this, having babies and changing diapers aren't things I want in a game. However looking through your work looks very thorough, I'm impressed, thank you for sharing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T21:09:18-07:00","id":1533467,"title":"","content":"I typed some words and erased them. I only need one:<br /> <br /> Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T21:28:06-07:00","id":1533468,"title":"","content":"The abstracted Childcare roll appears to have no\u2026 actual function?<br /> <br /> It's an extended roll with suggested modifiers and variable target success count (for which there's three substantially different totals that can all apply to a two-year-old) and no roll results, seemingly for the sole purposes of inflicting Conditions through the standard extended action rules for continuing after failure (there are no other mechanical consequences for failing the roll) <i>or</i> determining if the character(s) get through an eight-hour shift of childcare with time to spare (extended actions may have deadlines but don't typically represent a fixed amount of time overall save by multiplying the interval by the roll limit).<br /> <br /> I suspect the intent was not to make it so that characters without the Patient Merit and/or above-average Wits and Empathy are incapable of caring for a child for more than six hours due to the inability to roll more times than their base dicepool, just as I suspect the intent is mainly for successful Childcare rolls to represent keeping problems from occurring moreso than causing anything specific to happen, but the core system allows you to make repeated rolls for the same purpose without engaging with the systems for writing a screenplay or building a patio; the existing mechanics for staying awake through fatigue or resisting damage from disease and poisons serve an adequate precedent for &quot;roll every interval of time to stop problems from showing up or getting worse.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T15:02:02-07:00","id":1533499,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I suspect you missed the intention...<br /> <br /> What day was it yesterday ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T20:39:41-07:00","id":1533501,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea that you had. I personally lean more towards using children as PCs rather than as NPCs, but a group of individuals protecting a baby is a classic situation that is presented in literature. Due to a lack of knowledge regarding childcare, I cannot say if your mechanics are accurate to reality or not, but they seem like they would work in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T20:58:40-07:00","id":1533502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533499#post1533499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I suspect you missed the intention...</div> </div> </div> </div>Humor me. Go ahead, dissect the intention of the joke behind this document about childcare in a horror setting released on April Fool's Day having an abstracted roll that doesn't work like the type of roll it says it is. I'm very excited that you've volunteered to connect the dots and bring out the extra humor inherent in this lacuna, because it would sure be disappointing if the joke there was just &quot;it's bad on purpose&quot; in the middle of a twenty-odd page document that cites sources, links to another hundred-page document about playing child characters, and otherwise makes an effort to look like a serious attempt at mechanics for a mildly absurd premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T15:31:17-07:00","id":1533538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533467#post1533467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I typed some words and erased them. I only need one:<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well originally I had an idea for a Dark Era where the PCs are mere mortals trying to keep the very first reincarnated Princess alive and hopeful until the day she Blossoms. At first I thought I could just use a modified version of Satiety from BtP, but it rapidly became clear that would barely be scratching the surface, and would definitely not do justice to the incredible Herculean difficulties of parenting. So I read some books and watched some movies, let it all simmer for a few months, and this is the result. I realize not everyone will be into it and that's okay, I really just made it to satisfy my own creative itch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T15:51:17-07:00","id":1533540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533468#post1533468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The abstracted Childcare roll appears to have no\u2026 actual function?<br /> <br /> It's an extended roll with suggested modifiers and variable target success count (for which there's three substantially different totals that can all apply to a two-year-old) and no roll results, seemingly for the sole purposes of inflicting Conditions through the standard extended action rules for continuing after failure (there are no other mechanical consequences for failing the roll) <i>or</i> determining if the character(s) get through an eight-hour shift of childcare with time to spare (extended actions may have deadlines but don't typically represent a fixed amount of time overall save by multiplying the interval by the roll limit).<br /> <br /> I suspect the intent was not to make it so that characters without the Patient Merit and/or above-average Wits and Empathy are incapable of caring for a child for more than six hours due to the inability to roll more times than their base dicepool, just as I suspect the intent is mainly for successful Childcare rolls to represent keeping problems from occurring moreso than causing anything specific to happen, but the core system allows you to make repeated rolls for the same purpose without engaging with the systems for writing a screenplay or building a patio; the existing mechanics for staying awake through fatigue or resisting damage from disease and poisons serve an adequate precedent for &quot;roll every interval of time to stop problems from showing up or getting worse.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is why I posted the document on these forums: to get hard mechanical feedback like your excellent comment here. I can't believe I forgot to add roll results for the abstracted extended roll! I'm working on coming up with some specific results, but you're correct in assuming that the intention behind it was &quot;to represent keeping problems from occurring moreso than causing anything specific to happen&quot;. Your criticisms are all valid of course, and I need to review the RAW and do some deep thinking about how I want to modify them from here. I'm so glad that you pointed these issues out here, instead of letting me discover them at the gaming table with my friends!<br /> <br /> P.S. I actually didn't realize it was April Fools' Day when I posted it. Talk about bad timing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T06:02:36-07:00","id":1533558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533538#post1533538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well originally I had an idea for a Dark Era where the PCs are mere mortals trying to keep the very first reincarnated Princess alive and hopeful until the day she Blossoms. At first I thought I could just use a modified version of Satiety from BtP, but it rapidly became clear that would barely be scratching the surface, and would definitely not do justice to the incredible Herculean difficulties of parenting. So I read some books and watched some movies, let it all simmer for a few months, and this is the result. I realize not everyone will be into it and that's okay, I really just made it to satisfy my own creative itch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you actually use this in a game, with this granularity? What is the purpose of making the player roll dice to see how many actions it takes them to change a baby's diaper? Are they going to be changing the baby under duress? Rolling dice to see whether you catch the baby before she puts her hands into a cake? Conditions and sub-Conditions and stackable Conditions to measure different degrees of crying?<br /> <br /> As a general rule, every time you roll the dice, there should be a possibility of interesting consequences on a failure. If there aren't, don't roll them. (Extended actions don't apply this to every individual roll, but incline towards time pressure: roll the dice to see how many actions it takes when you're under duress and interesting consequences will follow if you don't get it done fast enough.) These are a lot of busywork rules that exist for the sake of having rules. Few of them actually help set up stories in play.<br /> <br /> The Carriage and Willpower sections are exceptions. They're more granular than I would prefer, but they are focused on dramatic situations where you might indeed be rolling dice to avoid interesting consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T11:08:11-07:00","id":1533565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533538#post1533538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well originally I had an idea for a Dark Era where the PCs are mere mortals trying to keep the very first reincarnated Princess alive and hopeful until the day she Blossoms. At first I thought I could just use a modified version of Satiety from BtP, but it rapidly became clear that would barely be scratching the surface, and would definitely not do justice to the incredible Herculean difficulties of parenting. So I read some books and watched some movies, let it all simmer for a few months, and this is the result. I realize not everyone will be into it and that's okay, I really just made it to satisfy my own creative itch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might we have access to this Dark Era, please? Having read the whole Doc, I'm now mightily interested in reading the work that drove you to make this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-04T12:16:50-07:00","id":1533568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533565#post1533565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might we have access to this Dark Era, please? Having read the whole Doc, I'm now mightily interested in reading the work that drove you to make this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with you. In general, I think that the idea of sheltering someone with a particularly powerful past incarnation is something that you could write interesting stories with. It sounds like the plot would thicken later on, when they reclaim some of their lost power or when their past life otherwise becomes more relevant. In any case, it is good to have mechanics for taking care of a young child. It seems like early childhood is an area that is not often covered, often in an understandable desire to cover what are often more narratively interesting ages later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T04:42:11-07:00","id":1533596,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533558#post1533558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a general rule, every time you roll the dice, there should be a possibility of interesting consequences on a failure. [...] These are a lot of busywork rules that exist for the sake of having rules. Few of them actually help set up stories in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of the intention behind the system, TBH. Parenthood is an enormous, permanent, and unending responsibility, and the only way to make that come across in a TTRPG is to make the players constantly roll for it. Admittedly, most groups would probably prefer to vastly simplify these rules or only have them come up when the need arises, but <i>if </i>they need to get granular then I've already drawn up some rules to help them do that. But maybe a sidebar about not making players roll unnecessarily is warranted; I'll jot one down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533565#post1533565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might we have access to this Dark Era, please? Having read the whole Doc, I'm now mightily interested in reading the work that drove you to make this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soon, my dearie duck, soon. You're not the only person to ask and while I'm eager to show off what I've written, the truth is it just isn't ready yet. There are a few more crucial '70s films I need to watch and NPCs I need to write, but rest assured I'm working on it whenever I can and I'll post the link here on the OP forums when it's done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T10:14:21-07:00","id":1533619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1533596#post1533596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soon, my dearie duck, soon. You're not the only person to ask and while I'm eager to show off what I've written, the truth is it just isn't ready yet. There are a few more crucial '70s films I need to watch and NPCs I need to write, but rest assured I'm working on it whenever I can and I'll post the link here on the OP forums when it's done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, whilst I'd prefer to see it sooner rather than later, take as long as you need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T19:52:04-07:00","id":1534568,"title":"","content":"why is i t not being shared more wideely I cant get my hands on the PDF I want<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-24T16:01:30-08:00","id":1547942,"title":"","content":"Oh theirs no rules ff=or the mentioned weekly stamina checks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T19:26:00-08:00","id":1548934,"title":"","content":"A perceptive reader pointed out that I never spelled out how the &quot;weekly Stamina roll&quot; mechanic actually works. Here is my attempt to remedy that oversight: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sickness</span><br /> At the end of each week, a child makes a Stamina roll to see whether it gets sick. Since babies and small children only possess a single dot of Stamina, this means that in \u2154 of cases they will fail this roll without outside assistance. Caregivers may spend Willpower to assist the child in this roll, but if they do and the child's roll fails then they cannot spend Willpower on their own Stamina + Resolve rolls to keep themselves from getting sick.<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><ul><li><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: The child takes one of the more serious Baby Conditions, detailed below; all caretakers make their own separate Stamina rolls to determine whether they contract the same illness as their child.</li> <li><b>Failure</b>: The child contracts a minor, common illness which is represented by the Sick Tilt (e.g. ear infection, sinus infection, pneumonia, persistent oral thrush, etc.); all caretakers make their own separate Stamina rolls to determine whether they contract the same illness as their child.</li> <li><b>Success</b>: The child manages to avoid getting sick\u2026 for now.</li> <li><b>Exceptional Success</b>: No special benefit.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Suggested Modifiers</b><ul><li>Child's sibling(s) is/are in school or daycare (-2)</li> <li>Child is in school or daycare (-3)</li> <li>The child and all of its caregivers have had little to no contact with other living humans in the previous week (+2)</li> <li>The child and/or its caregivers have had only moderate contact with outsiders in the previous week (+0)</li> <li>The child and/or its caregivers have had substantial contact with outsiders in the previous week (-2)</li> <li>The child and/or its caregivers have had extensive contact with large or densely-packed dense crowds of outsiders in the previous week (-4)<br /> </li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T15:20:09-08:00","id":1548969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1548934#post1548934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A perceptive reader pointed out that I never spelled out how the &quot;weekly Stamina roll&quot; mechanic actually works. Here is my attempt to remedy that oversight:[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually helps to clarify things quite a bit, thank you for the revision! Out of curiosity, does the weekly roll represent the actual chances of a child getting sick, or is that frequency more for narrative purposes, such as illnesses that might be relevant to a campaign featuring childcare?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T07:53:04-08:00","id":1548983,"title":"","content":"Well according to <a href=\"https://mcpress.mayoclinic.org/parenting/the-constant-cold-why-kids-are-always-sick-and-what-to-do-about-it/\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> from the Mayo Clinic, &quot;most babies, toddlers and preschoolers can have as many as 12 colds a year and still be normal. On average, you\u2019ll probably see between seven and eight infections a year&quot;! Failing two out of every three weekly Sickness rolls is probably a little more extreme than reality, but short of reintroducing the difficulty mechanics from OWoD (i.e., instead of adding or subtracting dice you raise or lower the threshold of what counts as a success) I'm not sure how to accurately represent this using NWoD/CofD mechanics.<br /> <br /> But since adults will almost always choose to spend Willpower on the child's behalf, they won't fail nearly that often. In fact, I kind of wonder if I've made it <i>too</i> easy to keep kids from getting sick, given how often it actually happens IRL. Maybe the willpower point should only add a single die, or none, to the child's Stamina roll? Or maybe the kid should only get sick on a dramatic failure (which will actually be pretty common, considering how easy it is for babies to take &quot;wound&quot; penalties from even a single point of bashing damage), and the willpower converts it back to a normal single-die roll? <br /> P.S. For those of you who have requested access to the <i>Just Before the Dawn</i> document, I'm happy to report that it's about 90% done; just a few more finishing touches to go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T14:21:34-08:00","id":1548993,"title":"","content":"Oh wow, that article actually gives a figure that had come to mind when the frequency of illness in children was brought up (going off of intuition, I figured that one check a month might be reasonable). With the odds of success and failure taken into consideration, I can see how the check per week works out, given how how unassisted, the child would probably still experience around nine illnesses a year. And yeah, the fixed difficulty ratings do prevent a degree of granularity from really being implemented, although all things considered the system that you present certainly still seems gameable. <br /> <br /> As for the subsystem, I think that the willpower point only providing one extra die would probably be the most workable solution? If you wanted it to be more in line with the vanilla game, you could potentially have it provide two dice, given how that is the norm for willpower augmenting Resistance rolls and the subsystem does involve Stamina, although that would obviously improve the odds of avoiding illness. Also, you actually raised a good point when it comes to wound penalties. Going by what is presented in the book, the child would have three health boxes in total (two from Size, and one from Stamina). As you said, any little bit of damage could severely impact their ability to resist illness, which I suppose actually makes sense, although it seems like it could be really debilitating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T15:05:21-07:00","id":1549532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>super_dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1533463-childcare-subsystem-\ud83d\udc76?p=1548983#post1548983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p.s. For those of you who have requested access to the <i>just before the dawn</i> document, i'm happy to report that it's about 90% done; just a few more finishing touches to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>whoop-whoop! Cultist of the light character, here i come!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-21T20:26:19-07:00","id":1560144,"title":"","content":"Id liike a cost given to babysitters nanny Private schoos daycare ccenters private schools sujpplys<br /> <br /> oh<br /> <br /> ooh andx tfolys and amujsement parks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-28T10:26:08-07:00","id":1560246,"title":"","content":"The following is to be taken with a heavy dose of salt, as I've just roughly skimmed the material.<br /> Seems mostly aligned with my experiences, although I'd say that things like feeding times and sleeping times can... vary. A lot.<br /> From &quot;I need to wake this baby every four to five hours so it eats, and it falls asleep almost directly afterwards, spending like 4 hours awake spread out over the whole day&quot; to &quot;this being is insatiable and constantly demands food, and will refuse anything that is not fresh breastmilk, to the point of prefering starvation over ingesting formula&quot; to &quot;why does it not sleep? WHYYY?!&quot;, everything can be part of parenthood experience. Possibly within the same child in the span of the first few months to a year. Standardizing makes is easier to handle for a game, for sure. But I guess you could just tack on a bunch of Conditions to reflect things like a permanently tired babe refusing to fall asleep (constantly at Mood -2 or -3, I suppose).<br /> <br /> While I wouldn't use this per se, I think this could be a very fun chronicle <i>hook</i>, either as a temporary escort-mission equivalent or as a short chronicle's focus. Something that might become one of those events that stay with the players long after due to being quite memorable, and also a &quot;let's not go through that again&quot; kind of thing.<br /> In fact, this could have been useful for an old chronicle (two Beasts had to deal with the fact their child was about to be born an Insatiable and needed to do an Obcasus Rite pre-birth but post-contractions to avoid that/exchange it for different problems). Throwing this at the two players would have been fun, even for a short amount of time. <br /> Especially if you as the ST know the rules but don't tell the players what they are, so they need to guesstimate. Just like it feels to be the case in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-14T09:15:22-07:00","id":1560620,"title":"","content":"in Right before the dawn should mortals with dreaam travel be eligible??<br /> <br /> <br /> Also is it safe tol say that doubling the cost of resources asides from being historically accurate is to keep players froom toppling difficulties wijth money hiring a nanny governess etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><im